From 5cfdccc7eb0b349df1ee8b179470beeb5c4fc203 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahriar Iravanian <siravan@svtsim.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:40:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] rusticol: defer the replay tile's momentum forms to the
 pacman runner (local, e2e)

When the runner fills the forms on the device (capability bit 1, with the sources there),
execute_replay_tile_from_external_planes no longer fills them on the CPU: it records the
external momenta and the selector's terms (permutation and momentum signs applied) for the
hook, which passes them to the runner, or fills the forms on the CPU exactly as before when
the plan run stays there. DirectWorkspace::momenta is now mutable for that fallback.
Tiles of one point and observed runs keep the eager fill. PACMAN_RECURRENCE_GPU_FORMS=0
disables it.
